9. Objective Function — Proxy Vector (No Scalarisation) — Corrected

Two-stage protocol.

Stage 1 — Pareto reconstruction. Compute the Pareto front \mathcal{P} via non-dominated sorting:

\mathcal{P} = \{x \in \mathcal{X} : \nexists\, x' \in \mathcal{X} \text{ s.t. } x' \succeq x,\; x' \neq x\}.

Stage 2 — Pre-registered decision rule. Select a single action only after the Pareto front is reported, using a pre-registered decision rule (e.g., entropy-weighted TOPSIS, knee-point selection, or lexicographic ordering on a designated primary objective). The rule and its parameters must be pre-registered before any experiment.

Objective Measurable proxy
J_{\text{truth}} ECE (with Brier co-primary); causal identification rate; replication rate
J_{\text{knowledge}} Expert-surprising discovery count; compression progress; mutual-information gain
J_{\text{flourishing}} Sen–Nussbaum capability achievement (≥3 measurable capabilities); health-adjusted autonomy; equity; institutional trust
Energy (three-tier) (i) Thermodynamic lower bound E \ge k_B T \ln 2; (ii) measured hardware energy; (iii) model-specific computational proxy
Risk \mathbb{E}[\text{harm}] \times P(\text{governance failure})

Solution concept. Pareto-optimal policies via chance-constrained or info-gap robust satisficing:

\min_{x \in \mathcal{X}} f(x) \quad \text{s.t.} \quad P(g(x, \xi) \le 0) \ge 1 - \epsilon.

If a scalar objective f(x) is used at all, it is used only in Stage 2 after the Pareto front is known, and the choice of f is pre-registered. No scalarisation is permitted in Stage 1.

