10.1 Arrow and Gibbard–Satterthwaite — acknowledged

Arrow's theorem: no social welfare function satisfies IIA, Pareto, and non-dictatorship simultaneously. Gibbard–Satterthwaite: every non-dictatorial, non-imposing voting rule with ≥3 alternatives is manipulable. We therefore sacrifice unrestricted domain for transitivity, adopting approval voting with exit rights as the second-best institution.

