G.1 Elicited Planning Assumptions

The probabilities in §8.9 (0.35, 0.40, 0.60, 0.30) are elicited planning assumptions, not empirical estimates. They are obtained via structured elicitation from the research team and are updated after every experiment. They must never be cited as evidence of actual risk levels.

G.2 Calibration Session Procedure

Elicitation sessions follow a structured protocol: (i) define the risk event operationally; (ii) provide base-rate information where available; (iii) elicit individual probabilities; (iv) discuss discrepancies; (v) record a consensus range and a point estimate. Sessions are documented and versioned.

G.3 Update Rule

After each experiment, elicited probabilities are updated using a simple Bayesian revision where the likelihood is derived from the observed event count and the prior is the elicited distribution. The update is reported alongside the original elicitation, preserving traceability.

