J.7 Energy Accounting: Three-Tier Separation

```
Tier I: Thermodynamic lower bound
        E >= k_B T ln 2 per irreversible bit erasure
        Not a measured quantity.
        Reversible computation is not subject to this bound.

Tier II: Measured hardware energy
        On-package power measurement at hardware package boundary.
        Reported in Joules per operation or Joules per inference.

Tier III: Model-specific computational proxy
        FLOPs, MACs, weighted operation count.
        Not a physical energy measure.
        Must never be presented as commensurable with Tier I or Tier II.

Joules per Bayesian surprise:

    E_surprise = E_measured / D_KL(p_post || p_prior)

Proposed GCRP 3 claim:
    reversible linear inference with ReLU-avoidance
    reduces E_surprise by >= 15% at fixed accuracy.
```

